    {
      "id": 25763,
      "nameEs": "Wing Commander IV: The Price of Freedom",
      "originalName": "Wing Commander IV: The Price of Freedom",
      "year": 1996,
      "igdbId": 934,
      "popularity": 24,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "best_version",
          "value": "64230",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Wing Commander IV: The Price of Freedom",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Wing Commander IV: The Price of Freedom",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Wing Commander 4 is one of the greatest space sims of all time, and some even consider it the greatest one of all. It is one of those games that did everything right. This is one of the few games that actually successfully manages to integrate a lot of FMV into the action, mostly because it uses trained film actors and directors. The combat is straightforward, fluid, and entertaining. The characters are as believable and memorable as they come. The orchestrated music -- just perfect. Finally, its enthralling story is both deep and plausible -- a combination that is often lost in modern games. There is simply no reason not to play this game and, once you do start playing, you will find it hard to think of a reason why you should stop.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Wing Commander 4 es uno de los mejores simuladores espaciales de todos los tiempos, e incluso algunos lo consideran el mejor de todos. Es uno de esos juegos que lo hicieron todo bien. Es de los pocos juegos que logran integrar con éxito una gran cantidad de FMV (secuencias de vídeo con actores reales) en la acción, sobre todo porque emplea actores y directores de cine con formación. El combate es directo, fluido y entretenido. Los personajes son tan creíbles y memorables como pueden serlo. La música orquestada: simplemente perfecta. Por último, su apasionante historia es profunda y verosímil, una combinación que a menudo se pierde en los juegos modernos. No hay ninguna razón para no jugarlo y, una vez que empiezas, te costará encontrar motivos para dejar de hacerlo.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1996",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
